I'd like to see more Lojbanists whose first language isn't Indo-European. T=
he=20
claim comes up frequently when there's a technical discussion that Lojban i=
s=20
Standard Average European. It's obvious from its grammar that it's not:
*All European languages have grammatical number. Lojban doesn't.
*Most European languages have accusative alignment. Basque has ergative=20
alignment. Lojban has an indefinitely long sequences of argument places,=20
which occurs in no natural language as far as I know.
*All European languages have nouns (including common nouns), verbs, and=20
adjectives, of which normally only verbs show tense. Lojban has no adjectiv=
es=20
and uses verbs, which show tense, for common nouns and adjectives as well a=
s=20
verbs.
I think that the appearance of SAE comes from most Lojbanists being native=
=20
speakers of European languages, and if we got more Lojbanists whose native=
=20
language have evidentials, tensed adjectives, and other non-European=20
features, the appearance would disappear.

I would like to see a few changes, such as:
*drop the dimension place from "mitre" and express it some other way which=
=20
would also work with "gucti"
*add x2 to "remna"
*allow BIhI to have only one GAhO (there is a construction that would have =
to=20
be disambiguated).

